 \\"data_table\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Player Form Scores\\",\\n      \\"columns\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\"header\\": \\"Player\\",\\n          \\"field\\": \\"player_name\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"text\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\"header\\": \\"Position\\", \\n          \\"field\\": \\"position\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"text\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\"header\\": \\"Form Score\\",\\n          \\"field\\": \\"form_score\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"number\\",\\n          \\"format\\": \\"decimal_1\\",\\n          \\"color_coding\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\"header\\": \\"Trend\\",\\n          \\"field\\": \\"form_trend\\", \\n          \\"type\\": \\"icon\\",\\n          \\"icons\\": {\\n            \\"up\\": \\"↗\\",\\n            \\"down\\": \\"↘\\", \\n            \\"stable\\": \\"→\\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\"header\\": \\"Games Played\\",\\n          \\"field\\": \\"recent_games_played\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"number\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\"header\\": \\"Last 5 Avg\\",\\n          \\"field\\": \\"last_5_avg_rating\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"number\\", \\n          \\"format\\": \\"decimal_1\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\"sorting\\": {\\n        \\"default_column\\": \\"form_score\\",\\n        \\"default_order\\": \\"desc\\"\\n      },\\n      \\"styling\\": {\\n        \\"color_thresholds\\": {\\n          \\"form_score\\": {\\n            \\"excellent\\": 8.0,\\n            \\"good\\": 6.5,\\n            \\"poor\\": 5.0\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Configuration\\nNow I need to generate a complete JSON configuration based on the user request for \\"Create a table with players and their form scores\\" and the planning I already have.\\n\\nLet me review the requirements:\\n1. Include 3-5 meaningful KPIs \\n2. Create 1-3 visualizations (charts or tables)\\n3. Each visualization must tell part of the story\\n4. Use appropriate visualization types - table is specifically requested\\n5. For tables, series should be column names \\n6. Time periods must be realistic (7/30/90 days)\\n\\nThe user wants a table showing players and their form scores. This is straightforward but I need to make it comprehensive.\\n\\n**Key considerations:**\\n- Form scores are typically based on recent performance, so I should use last30Days as the time period (gives enough games for meaningful form analysis)\\n- The primary visualization should be a table as requested\\n- KPIs should relate to form analysis - average form, top performers, players in good/poor form\\n- I could add a secondary visualization showing form trends over time\\n\\n**Story the data tells:**\\n- Who are the in-form players right now?\\n- How is the overall squad performing?\\n- Are there concerning drops in form?\\n- Which players are trending up/down?\\n\\n**KPIs to include:**\\n1. Average Team Form Score\\n2. Highest Form Score (player)\\n3. Players in Good Form (count)\\n4. Form Score Range (to show spread)\\n\\n**Visualizations:**\\n1. Primary: Table with players and form scores (as requested)\\n2. Secondary: Maybe a line chart showing form trends over time\\n\\nLet me structure this properly according to the format required:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"reportConfig\\": {\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Player Form Analysis\\",\\n    \\"timePeriod\\": \\"last30Days\\",\\n    \\"players\\": [\\"all\\"],\\n    \\"metrics\\": [\\"formScore\\", \\"performance\\"],\\n    \\"visualizationType\\": \\"table\\",\\n    \\"charts\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\"type\\": \\"table\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Player Form Scores\\",\\n        \\"xAxis\\": \\"player\\",\\n        \\"yAxis\\": \\"formScore\\", \\n        \\"series\\": [\\"playerName\\", \\"position\\", \\"formScore\\", \\"trend\\", \\"gamesPlayed\\", \\"recentAverage\\"]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"type\\": \\"line\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Form Score Trends\\",\\n        \\"xAxis\\": \\"date\\",\\n        \\"yAxis\\": \\"formScore\\",\\n        \\"series\\": [\\"topPerformers\\", \\"averageForm\\"]\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\"kpis\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\"label\\": \\"Average Team Form Score\\",\\n        \\"value\\": 0\\n\\nI'll continue the JSON configuration by completing the KPI section with specific metrics that provide insights into the team's performance and individual player form.\\n\\nThe KPIs capture key performance indicators like overall team form, top performers, players in good form, and the range of form scores. Each metric offers a different perspective on the squad's current performance level, helping coaches and analysts quickly assess the team's condition.\\n\\nI'll focus on creating a visualization that highlights these nuanced performance metrics, ensuring the time frame and chart type align with meaningful performance analysis.\\nLooking at the request for a player form table, I need to create a comprehensive report that provides insights into current player performance levels.\\n\\n## Analysis & Planning\\n\\n**Data Story**: This report will help identify which players are currently in good form versus those who may be struggling, based on recent performance data.\\n\\n**Key Insights Needed**:\\n- Individual player form rankings for easy comparison\\n- Overall squad form health metrics\\n- Identification of top performers and players needing attention\\n- Performance trends to show if players are improving or declining\\n\\n**Visualization Strategy**:\\n- Primary: Data table showing detailed player form information (as requested)\\n- Secondary: Trend visualization to show form patterns over time\\n\\n**Time Period**: 30 days provides enough recent matches to calculate meaningful form scores while staying current.\\n\\n**Critical Metrics**: Form scores, recent performance averages, trend indicators, and contextual information like position and games played.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"reportCo