cmiyso44g0001bkswbaxxdsdc	Generate a performance report for active_players f...	reports	ready	Generate a performance report for active_players focusing on wellness_score, load, rpe, presenting insights through kpi_cards, charts, summary_text with data from training_management, wearable_tech over last_30_days.	{"reportConfig": {"kpis": [{"label": "Average Wellness Score", "trend": "up", "value": "N/A (connect to data)", "format": "number", "description": "Team average wellness for 30-day period"}, {"label": "Average Training Load", "trend": "neutral", "value": "N/A (connect to data)", "format": "number", "description": "Average daily training load per player"}, {"label": "Average RPE Score", "trend": "down", "value": "N/A (connect to data)", "format": "number", "description": "Rate of perceived exertion average"}, {"label": "Players at Risk", "trend": "down", "value": "N/A (connect to data)", "format": "number", "description": "Players with poor wellness-load balance"}], "title": "Player Performance & Wellness Report - 30 Day Analysis", "charts": [{"type": "line", "title": "Wellness Score Trends Over Time", "xAxis": "date", "yAxis": "score", "series": ["wellness", "fatigue"]}, {"type": "bar", "title": "Player Training Load Comparison", "xAxis": "player", "yAxis": "load", "series": ["trainingLoad"]}, {"type": "area", "title": "RPE Accumulation Over Time", "xAxis": "date", "yAxis": "rpe", "series": ["rpe", "cumulativeRPE"]}], "metrics": ["wellness", "trainingLoad", "rpe", "performance"], "players": ["all"], "timePeriod": "last30Days"}}	{"response": "\\n\\n## Planning\\nLet me analyze this request carefully:\\n\\n**User Request Analysis:**\\n- **Focus**: Active players\\n- **Key Metrics**: wellness_score, load, rpe (rate of perceived exertion)\\n- **Data Sources**: training_management, wearable_tech\\n- **Time Period**: last_30_days\\n- **Presentation**: KPI cards, charts, summary text\\n\\n**What story does the data need to tell?**\\nThis report needs to tell the story of player wellness and training load management over the past month. It should help coaches and sports scientists understand:\\n1. Overall wellness trends across the team\\n2. Training load distribution and patterns\\n3. How players are perceiving their exertion levels\\n4. Any correlations between wellness, load, and RPE\\n5. Identify players who might be at risk of overtraining or underperforming\\n\\n**Which chart types best suit each metric?**\\n1. **Wellness Score**: \\n   - Time series line chart to show trends over 30 days\\n   - Box plot or violin plot to show distribution across players\\n   - Heatmap to show individual player wellness over time\\n\\n2. **Load**: \\n   - Time series line chart for load trends\\n   - Bar chart for average load by player\\n   - Scatter plot comparing load vs wellness or RPE\\n\\n3. **RPE**: \\n   - Time series line chart for RPE trends\\n   - Histogram showing RPE distribution\\n   - Correlation scatter plot with load or wellness\\n\\n4. **Combined Analysis**:\\n   - Multi-line chart showing all three metrics over time\\n   - Correlation matrix heatmap\\n   - Player comparison radar/spider chart\\n\\n**What KPIs matter most?**\\n1. **Average Wellness Score** (last 30 days vs previous period)\\n2. **Average Training Load** (last 30 days vs previous period)\\n3. **Average RPE** (last 30 days vs previous period)\\n4. **Wellness-Load Correlation** (how well balanced is the training?)\\n\\n\\n5. **Players at Risk** (count of players with concerning metrics)\\n6. **Peak Load Day** (highest load day in the period)\\n\\nI'll design a comprehensive dashboard layout that provides a holistic view of player performance and wellness. The visualization strategy will focus on creating an intuitive, data-driven narrative that allows quick insights into team and individual athlete conditions. By combining multiple chart types and metrics, we can create a robust analysis tool for sports performance management.\\n\\nThe dashboard will prioritize visual clarity, using color-coded indicators and trend lines to highlight critical information. Interactive elements will allow coaches to drill down into specific player data, making the complex dataset accessible and actionable.\\n\\n**KPI Cards and Charts** will include wellness scores, training load metrics, RPE indicators, and risk assessment visualizations. The multi-layered approach ensures comprehensive performance tracking across individual and team levels.\\n\\n**Key Visualization Strategies:**\\n1. Color-coded risk indicators\\n2. Trend-based performance tracking\\n3. Comparative player analysis\\n4. Correlation-driven insights\\n\\n**Configuration Framework:**\\n- Dynamic data mapping\\n- Flexible metric thresholds\\n- Automated player risk scoring\\n- Adaptive visualization parameters\\nLooking at this request, I need to create a comprehensive performance report focusing on player wellness management. Let me analyze the key requirements:\\n\\n**Story to Tell:**\\n- How are active players managing training load and wellness over the past month?\\n- Are players maintaining good wellness while handling appropriate training loads?\\n- What's the relationship between perceived exertion and actual training metrics?\\n- Which players might need attention for recovery or load management?\\n\\n**Visualization Strategy:**\\n- Time series charts for trend analysis over 30 days\\n- Correlation charts to understand relationships between metrics\\n- Player-level comparisons to identify outliers\\n- Risk assessment visualizations\\n\\n**Key Performance Indicators:**\\n- Average wellness, load, and RPE with trend comparisons\\n- Correlation coefficients between metrics\\n- Risk indicators for overtraining or poor recovery\\n\\n**Layout Flow:**\\n1. High-level KPIs across the top\\n2. Trend analysis in the middle sections\\n3. Player-level and correlation analysis\\n4. Summary insights and recommendations\\n\\nHere's the planned configuration:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"reportConfig\\": {\\n    \\"sections\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"kpi_overview\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"kpi_cards\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Performance Overview - Last 30 Days\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"columns\\": 6,\\n          \\"height\\": \\"compact\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"cards\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"avg_wellness\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Average Wellness Score\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"wellness_score\\",\\n            \\"aggregation\\": \\"average\\",\\n            \\"comparison\\": {\\n              \\"period\\": \\"previous_30_days\\",\\n              \\"type\\": \\"percentage_change\\"\\n            },\\n            \\"format\\": \\"decimal_1\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 7.0,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"higher_better\\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"avg_load\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Average Training Load\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"load\\",\\n            \\"aggregation\\": \\"average\\",\\n            \\"comparison\\": {\\n              \\"period\\": \\"previous_30_days\\",\\n              \\"type\\": \\"percentage_change\\"\\n            },\\n            \\"format\\": \\"integer\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"avg_rpe\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Average RPE\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"rpe\\",\\n            \\"aggregation\\": \\"average\\",\\n            \\"comparison\\": {\\n              \\"period\\": \\"previous_30_days\\",\\n              \\"type\\": \\"percentage_change\\"\\n            },\\n            \\"format\\": \\"decimal_1\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 6.0,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"optimal_range\\",\\n              \\"range\\": [4.0, 7.0]\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"wellness_load_correlation\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Wellness-Load Correlation\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"correlation\\",\\n            \\"calculation\\": \\"correlation(wellness_score, load)\\",\\n            \\"format\\": \\"decimal_2\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 0.3,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"higher_better\\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"high_risk_players\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Players at Risk\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"players_count\\",\\n            \\"filter\\": \\"wellness_score < 6.0 OR (load > average_load * 1.3 AND rpe > 7.5)\\",\\n            \\"format\\": \\"integer\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 0,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"lower_better\\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"peak_load_days\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"High Load Days\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"days_count\\",\\n            \\"filter\\": \\"load > (SELECT AVG(load) * 1.5 FROM training_management WHERE date >= NOW() - INTERVAL 30 DAY)\\",\\n            \\"format\\": \\"integer\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"wellness_trends\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"line_chart\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Wellness Score Trends\\",\\n        \\"data_source\\": [\\"training_management\\", \\"wearable_tech\\"],\\n        \\"x_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"date\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"datetime\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Date\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"y_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"wellness_score\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Wellness Score\\",\\n          \\"range\\": [1, 10]\\n        },\\n        \\"grouping\\": \\"player_id\\",\\n        \\"aggregation\\": \\"daily_average\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"half\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"medium\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"styling\\": {\\n          \\"show_average_line\\": true,\\n          \\"show_target_zone\\": true,\\n          \\"target_zone\\": [6.5, 8.5]\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"load_trends\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"line_chart\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Training Load Trends\\",\\n        \\"data_source\\": [\\"training_management\\"],\\n        \\"x_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"date\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"datetime\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Date\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"y_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"load\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Training Load\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"grouping\\": \\"team_average\\",\\n        \\"aggregation\\": \\"daily_sum\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"half\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"medium\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"styling\\": {\\n          \\"show_average_line\\": true,\\n          \\"show_trend_line\\": true\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"rpe_patterns\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"combination_chart\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"RPE vs Training Load Patterns\\",\\n        \\"data_source\\": [\\"training_management\\"],\\n        \\"x_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"date\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"datetime\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Date\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"y_axes\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\"field\\": \\"rpe\\",\\n            \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"RPE\\",\\n            \\"chart_type\\": \\"line\\",\\n            \\"side\\": \\"left\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"field\\": \\"load\\",\\n            \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Load\\",\\n            \\"chart_type\\": \\"column\\",\\n            \\"side\\": \\"right\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\"aggregation\\": \\"daily_average\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"full\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"medium\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"player_wellness_heatmap\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"heatmap\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Individual Player Wellness Patterns\\",\\n        \\"data_source\\": [\\"training_management\\", \\"wearable_tech\\"],\\n        \\"x_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"date\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"datetime\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Date\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"y_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"player_name\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"categorical\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Player\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"value_field\\": \\"wellness_score\\",\\n        \\"color_scale\\": {\\n          \\"type\\": \\"traffic_light\\",\\n          \\"low\\": {\\"value\\": 5, \\"color\\": \\"red\\"},\\n          \\"medium\\": {\\"value\\": 7, \\"color\\": \\"yellow\\"},\\n          \\"high\\": {\\"value\\": 9, \\"color\\": \\"green\\"}\\n        },\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"half\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"large\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"load_wellness_correlation\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"scatter_plot\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Load vs Wellness Correlation\\",\\n        \\"data_source\\": [\\"training_management\\", \\"wearable_tech\\"],\\n        \\"x_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"load\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Training Load\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"y_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"wellness_score\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Wellness Score\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"grouping\\": \\"player_id\\",\\n        \\"sizing\\": \\"rpe\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"half\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"large\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"styling\\": {\\n          \\"show_trend_line\\": true,\\n          \\"show_correlation_coefficient\\": true\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"player_comparison\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"bar_chart\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Player Performance Comparison\\",\\n        \\"data_source\\": [\\"training_management\\", \\"wearable_tech\\"],\\n        \\"x_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"player_name\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"categorical\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Player\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"y_axis\\": {\\n          \\"field\\": \\"composite_score\\",\\n          \\"calculation\\": \\"(wellness_score * 0.4) + ((10 - rpe) * 0.3) + (normalized_load * 0.3)\\",\\n          \\"type\\": \\"numeric\\",\\n          \\"title\\": \\"Performance Index\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"sorting\\": \\"descending\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"full\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"medium\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"styling\\": {\\n          \\"color_by_value\\": true,\\n          \\"show_data_labels\\": true\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"summary_insights\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"summary_text\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Key Insights & Recommendations\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"width\\": \\"full\\",\\n          \\"height\\": \\"compact\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"content\\": {\\n          \\"auto_generate\\": true,\\n          \\"focus_areas\\": [\\n            \\"wellness_trends\\",\\n            \\"load_management\\",\\n            \\"player_risk_assessment\\",\\n            \\"rpe_load_balance\\",\\n            \\"recommendations\\"\\n          ],\\n          \\"include_statistics\\": true\\n        }\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\"filters\\": {\\n      \\"date_range\\": {\\n        \\"type\\": \\"last_n_days\\",\\n        \\"value\\": 30\\n      },\\n      \\"player_status\\": \\"active\\",\\n      \\"data_sources\\": [\\"training_management\\", \\"wearable_tech\\"]\\n    },\\n    \\"refresh_schedule\\": \\"daily\\",\\n    \\"export_options\\": [\\"pdf\\", \\"excel\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Configuration\\nLet me analyze this request carefully and generate a proper JSON configuration following the specific requirements:\\n\\n**User Request Analysis:**\\n- Focus: Active players \\n- Key Metrics: wellness_score, load, rpe (rate of perceived exertion)\\n- Data Sources: training_management, wearable_tech\\n- Time Period: last_30_days\\n- Presentation: KPI cards, charts, summary text\\n\\n**Story the data needs to tell:**\\nThis report needs to help coaches understand how players are managing training load and wellness over the past month. Key questions:\\n1. Are players maintaining good wellness while handling training loads?\\n2. How do players perceive their exertion relative to actual load?\\n3. Which players need attention for recovery or load management?\\n4. What are the trends and patterns over the 30-day period?\\n\\n**CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS I MUST FOLLOW:**\\n1. **KPIs**: Include EXACTLY 3-5 meaningful KPIs \\n2. **Charts**: Create EXACTLY 1-3 visualizations (NEVER more than 3)\\n3. **Chart Variety**: Use DIFFERENT chart types - NEVER use the same type for all charts\\n4. **Time Period**: Use \\"last30Days\\" format\\n\\n**KPI Selection (4 KPIs):**\\n1. Average Wellness Score - key metric for overall player condition\\n2. Average Training Load - understanding workload management  \\n3. Average RPE - perception of exertion levels\\n4. Wellness-Load Balance - players at risk indicator\\n\\n**Chart Selection (3 different types):**\\n1. **Line Chart**: Wellness Score trends over time - shows temporal patterns\\n2. **Bar Chart**: Player comparison for training loads - shows categorical comparisons  \\n3. **Area Chart**: RPE trends over time with cumulative perspective\\n\\nThis gives me 3 different chart types with distinct purposes:\\n- Line: trends over time\\n- Bar: comparisons between categories\\n- Area: cumulative data over time\\n\\nLet me structure this properly:\\n\\n\\nI'll start configuring the JSON to capture the comprehensive player performance and wellness analysis. The configuration will include a detailed breakdown of metrics, chart types, and visualization requirements to provide coaches with a holistic view of player conditions over the past 30 days.\\n\\nThe report design incorporates multiple visualization strategies: line charts for wellness score tracking, bar graphs for comparative training load assessment, and area charts to monitor RPE accumulation. Each chart is strategically designed to reveal nuanced performance insights across different dimensions.\\n\\nKey performance indicators will highlight critical team-level metrics, enabling quick assessment of overall player wellness and training intensity. The flexible configuration allows for dynamic data connection and real-time performance monitoring.\\n\\nThe dashboard emphasizes comparative analysis, tracking individual and aggregate training metrics to support proactive athlete management and performance optimization strategies.\\n\\nI'll focus on three distinct visualization approaches: line charts for tracking temporal progression, bar charts for categorical comparisons, and area charts to illustrate cumulative training load dynamics. Each chart type provides a unique analytical perspective on athlete performance and wellness.\\nLooking at this request, I need to create a performance report that tells the story of how active players are managing training load, wellness, and perceived exertion over the past month. This data will help coaches identify trends, spot potential issues, and make informed decisions about player management.\\n\\n**Key Story Elements:**\\n- Overall team wellness trends and patterns\\n- Training load distribution across players\\n- Relationship between perceived exertion and actual metrics\\n- Risk identification for overtraining or poor recovery\\n\\n**Visualization Strategy:**\\n1. **Time-based trends** to show how metrics evolve over the 30-day period\\n2. **Player comparisons** to identify outliers and individual patterns  \\n3. **Cumulative analysis** to understand workload accumulation\\n\\n**KPI Focus:**\\n- Core wellness and performance metrics\\n- Risk indicators for player management\\n- Trend comparisons for decision-making context\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"reportConfig\\": {\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Player Performance & Wellness Report - 30 Day Analysis\\",\\n    \\"timePeriod\\": \\"last30Days\\",\\n    \\"players\\": [\\"all\\"],\\n    \\"metrics\\": [\\"wellness\\", \\"trainingLoad\\", \\"rpe\\", \\"performance\\"],\\n    \\"charts\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\"type\\": \\"line\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Wellness Score Trends Over Time\\",\\n        \\"xAxis\\": \\"date\\",\\n        \\"yAxis\\": \\"score\\",\\n        \\"series\\": [\\"wellness\\", \\"fatigue\\"]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"type\\": \\"bar\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Player Training Load Comparison\\",\\n        \\"xAxis\\": \\"player\\",\\n        \\"yAxis\\": \\"load\\",\\n        \\"series\\": [\\"trainingLoad\\"]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"type\\": \\"area\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"RPE Accumulation Over Time\\",\\n        \\"xAxis\\": \\"date\\",\\n        \\"yAxis\\": \\"rpe\\",\\n        \\"series\\": [\\"rpe\\", \\"cumulativeRPE\\"]\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\"kpis\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\"label\\": \\"Average Wellness Score\\",\\n        \\"value\\": \\"N/A (connect to data)\\",\\n        \\"format\\": \\"number\\",\\n        \\"trend\\": \\"up\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Team average wellness for 30-day period\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"label\\": \\"Average Training Load\\",\\n        \\"value\\": \\"N/A (connect to data)\\",\\n        \\"format\\": \\"number\\",\\n        \\"trend\\": \\"neutral\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Average daily training load per player\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"label\\": \\"Average RPE Score\\",\\n        \\"value\\": \\"N/A (connect to data)\\",\\n        \\"format\\": \\"number\\",\\n        \\"trend\\": \\"down\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Rate of perceived exertion average\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"label\\": \\"Players at Risk\\",\\n        \\"value\\": \\"N/A (connect to data)\\",\\n        \\"format\\": \\"number\\",\\n        \\"trend\\": \\"down\\",\\n        \\"description\\": \\"Players with poor wellness-load balance\\"\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n```", "reasoning": "\\n\\n## Planning\\nLet me analyze this request carefully:\\n\\n**User Request Analysis:**\\n- **Focus**: Active players\\n- **Key Metrics**: wellness_score, load, rpe (rate of perceived exertion)\\n- **Data Sources**: training_management, wearable_tech\\n- **Time Period**: last_30_days\\n- **Presentation**: KPI cards, charts, summary text\\n\\n**What story does the data need to tell?**\\nThis report needs to tell the story of player wellness and training load management over the past month. It should help coaches and sports scientists understand:\\n1. Overall wellness trends across the team\\n2. Training load distribution and patterns\\n3. How players are perceiving their exertion levels\\n4. Any correlations between wellness, load, and RPE\\n5. Identify players who might be at risk of overtraining or underperforming\\n\\n**Which chart types best suit each metric?**\\n1. **Wellness Score**: \\n   - Time series line chart to show trends over 30 days\\n   - Box plot or violin plot to show distribution across players\\n   - Heatmap to show individual player wellness over time\\n\\n2. **Load**: \\n   - Time series line chart for load trends\\n   - Bar chart for average load by player\\n   - Scatter plot comparing load vs wellness or RPE\\n\\n3. **RPE**: \\n   - Time series line chart for RPE trends\\n   - Histogram showing RPE distribution\\n   - Correlation scatter plot with load or wellness\\n\\n4. **Combined Analysis**:\\n   - Multi-line chart showing all three metrics over time\\n   - Correlation matrix heatmap\\n   - Player comparison radar/spider chart\\n\\n**What KPIs matter most?**\\n1. **Average Wellness Score** (last 30 days vs previous period)\\n2. **Average Training Load** (last 30 days vs previous period)\\n3. **Average RPE** (last 30 days vs previous period)\\n4. **Wellness-Load Correlation** (how well balanced is the training?)\\n\\n\\n5. **Players at Risk** (count of players with concerning metrics)\\n6. **Peak Load Day** (highest load day in the period)\\n\\nI'll design a comprehensive dashboard layout that provides a holistic view of player performance and wellness. The visualization strategy will focus on creating an intuitive, data-driven narrative that allows quick insights into team and individual athlete conditions. By combining multiple chart types and metrics, we can create a robust analysis tool for sports performance management.\\n\\nThe dashboard will prioritize visual clarity, using color-coded indicators and trend lines to highlight critical information. Interactive elements will allow coaches to drill down into specific player data, making the complex dataset accessible and actionable.\\n\\n**KPI Cards and Charts** will include wellness scores, training load metrics, RPE indicators, and risk assessment visualizations. The multi-layered approach ensures comprehensive performance tracking across individual and team levels.\\n\\n**Key Visualization Strategies:**\\n1. Color-coded risk indicators\\n2. Trend-based performance tracking\\n3. Comparative player analysis\\n4. Correlation-driven insights\\n\\n**Configuration Framework:**\\n- Dynamic data mapping\\n- Flexible metric thresholds\\n- Automated player risk scoring\\n- Adaptive visualization parameters\\nLooking at this request, I need to create a comprehensive performance report focusing on player wellness management. Let me analyze the key requirements:\\n\\n**Story to Tell:**\\n- How are active players managing training load and wellness over the past month?\\n- Are players maintaining good wellness while handling appropriate training loads?\\n- What's the relationship between perceived exertion and actual training metrics?\\n- Which players might need attention for recovery or load management?\\n\\n**Visualization Strategy:**\\n- Time series charts for trend analysis over 30 days\\n- Correlation charts to understand relationships between metrics\\n- Player-level comparisons to identify outliers\\n- Risk assessment visualizations\\n\\n**Key Performance Indicators:**\\n- Average wellness, load, and RPE with trend comparisons\\n- Correlation coefficients between metrics\\n- Risk indicators for overtraining or poor recovery\\n\\n**Layout Flow:**\\n1. High-level KPIs across the top\\n2. Trend analysis in the middle sections\\n3. Player-level and correlation analysis\\n4. Summary insights and recommendations\\n\\nHere's the planned configuration:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"reportConfig\\": {\\n    \\"sections\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"kpi_overview\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"kpi_cards\\",\\n        \\"title\\": \\"Performance Overview - Last 30 Days\\",\\n        \\"layout\\": {\\n          \\"columns\\": 6,\\n          \\"height\\": \\"compact\\"\\n        },\\n        \\"cards\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"avg_wellness\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Average Wellness Score\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"wellness_score\\",\\n            \\"aggregation\\": \\"average\\",\\n            \\"comparison\\": {\\n              \\"period\\": \\"previous_30_days\\",\\n              \\"type\\": \\"percentage_change\\"\\n            },\\n            \\"format\\": \\"decimal_1\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 7.0,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"higher_better\\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"avg_load\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Average Training Load\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"load\\",\\n            \\"aggregation\\": \\"average\\",\\n            \\"comparison\\": {\\n              \\"period\\": \\"previous_30_days\\",\\n              \\"type\\": \\"percentage_change\\"\\n            },\\n            \\"format\\": \\"integer\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"avg_rpe\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Average RPE\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"rpe\\",\\n            \\"aggregation\\": \\"average\\",\\n            \\"comparison\\": {\\n              \\"period\\": \\"previous_30_days\\",\\n              \\"type\\": \\"percentage_change\\"\\n            },\\n            \\"format\\": \\"decimal_1\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 6.0,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"optimal_range\\",\\n              \\"range\\": [4.0, 7.0]\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"wellness_load_correlation\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Wellness-Load Correlation\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"correlation\\",\\n            \\"calculation\\": \\"correlation(wellness_score, load)\\",\\n            \\"format\\": \\"decimal_2\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 0.3,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"higher_better\\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"high_risk_players\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"Players at Risk\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"players_count\\",\\n            \\"filter\\": \\"wellness_score < 6.0 OR (load > average_load * 1.3 AND rpe > 7.5)\\",\\n            \\"format\\": \\"integer\\",\\n            \\"target\\": {\\n              \\"value\\": 0,\\n              \\"comparison\\": \\"lower_better\\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\"id\\": \\"peak_load_days\\",\\n            \\"title\\": \\"High Load Days\\",\\n            \\"metric\\": \\"days_count\\",\\n            \\"filter\\": \\"load > (SELECT AVG(load) * 1.5 FROM training_management WHERE date >= NOW() - INTERVAL 30 DAY)\\",\\n            \\"format\\": \\"integer\\"\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\"id\\": \\"wellness_trends\\",\\n        \\"type\\": \\"